{"id":"NCT04199403","title":"Assessment of Complication Risk Factors in a French National Cohort of Asplenic Patients","official":"Assessment of Complication Risk Factors in a French National Cohort of Asplenic Patients","summary":"Spleen could have been surgically removed for trauma, cancer, auto-immune disease, or to perform a diagnosis. Spleen could be non-functional due to radiotherapy or splenic artery embolism. These patients are at risks of infectious diseases due to encapsulated bacteria, cancer, and thromboembolism disease. The purpose of this study is to assess complications occurring in French patients without spleen and to implement new diagnostic tools for follow-up.","conditions":["Asplenia"],"interventions":[],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* ≥18 year-old\n* With asplenia due to splenectomy, splenic artery embolization or radiotherapy\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Genetic asplenia including sick cell disease","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":6000,"start":"2020-01-09","pcd":"2040-01","upd":"2026-07-16","sponsor":"Poitiers University Hospital","areas":["other"],"central":["Mathieu PUYADE, MD · +33 5 49 44 32 76 · mathieu.puyade@chu-poitiers.fr","Corinne Lorrain · +33 5 49 44 39 30 · corinne.lorrain@chu-poitiers.fr"],"sites":[{"f":"C.H. d'Angoulême","city":"Angoulême","pr":"","zip":"16959","s":"R","lat":45.65,"lon":0.1535,"c":"Agnès RICHE, MD · agnes.riche@ch-angouleme.fr"},{"f":"C.H. Victor Dupouy","city":"Argenteuil","pr":"","zip":"95100","s":"R","lat":48.9479,"lon":2.2474,"c":"Damien CONTOU, MD · +33 1 34 23 11 73 · damien.contou@ch-argenteuil.fr"},{"f":"C.H. de Béthune","city":"Béthune","pr":"","zip":"62660","s":"STOP","lat":50.5296,"lon":2.64,"c":""},{"f":"Hôpitaux de Chartres","city":"Chartres","pr":"","zip":"28019","s":"ANR","lat":48.4468,"lon":1.4892,"c":""},{"f":"C.H.U. de Lille","city":"Lille","pr":"","zip":"59037","s":"R","lat":50.6339,"lon":3.0551,"c":"Fanny VU